# LangChain Runtime & LangGraph integration (overview)

What was added
- langchain_runtime/: a FastAPI-based LangChain runtime that integrates your AegisLLM/AgentRunner,
  calls your retrieval service, attaches MCP context, exposes /v1/chain/run and emits Prometheus metrics.
- langgraph/: a small graph-planning service using RedisGraph (or networkx fallback) providing /plan endpoint.
- An adapter in the LangChain runtime calls your existing AgentRunner when LangChain or advanced agents aren't necessary.
- Demo script and CI smoke workflow to validate the runtime endpoint.

Deployment notes
- Build and push Docker images or replace <YOUR_REGISTRY> placeholders in Helm values.
- Deploy RedisGraph (or the Redis + redisgraph module) if you want full graph persistence; else use in-memory.
- Wire AEGIS_MCP_API and AEGIS_RETRIEVAL_API env variables to point to your MCP & retrieval services.
- Ensure A2A / approver API endpoint is reachable for approval requests.

Security & production
- Add auth (JWT) and RBAC to the LangChain runtime and LangGraph service.
- Configure rate limits and OPA pre-flight checks for agent execution.
- Use GPU-backed nodes and vLLM/Triton when running large models in production.
